        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "You can support platelet recovery at home during dengue by drinking plenty of fluids, eating nutrient-rich foods, and getting complete rest.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "drinking plenty of fluids, eating nutrient-rich foods, and getting complete rest"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Hydration and Fluids"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Drink 2 to 3 liters of fluids daily to maintain blood volume and prevent dehydration."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Sip on coconut water for essential electrolytes and minerals."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Include oral rehydration solutions (ORS), clear soups, and fresh fruit juices."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          2,
          3
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Platelet-Supporting Foods"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Drink Papaya Leaf Extract, which contains enzymes that traditional use and studies suggest help boost platelet production. Crush fresh leaves, extract the juice, and take small amounts (like 2 tablespoons) twice daily.",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "text": "Papaya Leaf Extract",
                "link": "https://www.justdial.com/Ahmedabad/Papaya-Leaf-Dealers/nct-11201565"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Eat Vitamin C-rich foods like oranges, amla (Indian gooseberry), lemons, and kiwi to strengthen immunity and support cell regeneration."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Consume iron and folate-rich foods like spinach, beetroot, and pomegranate to help with blood cell production."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Eat Vitamin A-rich sweet pumpkin and its seeds to support platelet formation in the bone marrow."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          4,
          5,
          6
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Crucial Precautions and Care"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Get complete bed rest so your immune system can focus on fighting the virus."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Avoid blood-thinning medications like aspirin and ibuprofen, which can worsen bleeding risks. Use only doctor-recommended paracetamol for fever."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Monitor your platelet counts with regular blood tests."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2,
          7
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Seek immediate medical care if your platelet count drops below 50,000, if you see warning signs like bleeding gums, nosebleeds, severe abdominal pain, or black stools, or if you feel extreme fatigue. You can review Max Healthcare or Sarvodaya Hospital for additional medical guidelines on managing dengue recovery.",
